# AvalynxOffice Source-Available License (Draft)

**Status: LEGAL_REVIEW_REQUIRED — this is a draft for review by legal counsel.
It is not a finally binding legal document.**

Version: 1.0-DRAFT — Copyright (c) 2026 JBS New Media GmbH

## 1. Grant

Subject to the terms below, the copyright holder grants you a non-exclusive,
non-transferable, worldwide right to use, copy, modify and create derivative
works of this software (the "AvalynxOffice") for the purpose of operating a
self-hosted groupware installation (e-mail, calendars, contacts).

## 2. Free Community Use

Use of the software is free of charge for installations with **up to three (3)
counted user accounts** ("Seats"). All functions are technically identical;
there are no feature tiers.

## 3. Commercial Use

An installation with **more than three (3) Seats** requires a commercial
license agreement with the copyright holder. Commercial licenses are additive:
each valid license grants an additional number of Seats on top of the three
free Seats. Deactivated and deleted user accounts do not count as Seats.
Technical service accounts without personal access are excluded.

Licenses must not be combined across different organizations. Duplicate
license keys with identical license identifiers are only counted once.

For associations, non-profit organizations and educational institutions there
is **no** automatic free special license. Individual special licenses can be
requested separately and are granted at the sole discretion of the copyright
holder.

## 4. Technical Enforcement

The software contains technical measures that count Seats and — after a grace
period of 30 days following a license violation — restrict the software to a
read-only mode for user-initiated write operations. Receiving, storing and
reading e-mails remain possible in read-only mode; sending and modifications
to e-mails, calendars and contacts are disabled. These technical measures do
not create, limit or extend any contractual rights; the decisive terms are
those of the applicable (commercial) license agreement.

## 5. Restrictions

You must not:

1. use the software in production with more than three Seats without a valid
   commercial license;
2. circumvent, disable or modify the technical license enforcement;
3. remove or alter copyright, trademark or attribution notices;
4. redistribute the software or derivative works except under the terms of
   this license.

## 6. Source Availability and Change License

This license follows the *source-available* model: the source code is publicly
viewable but is not licensed under an OSI-approved open-source license.

The copyright holder intends to release each version of the software under an
OSI-approved open-source license (the "Change License") no later than four
years after the first availability of that version (the "Change Date"). The
intended Change License is **planned** to be the **GNU Affero General Public
License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0)** — this choice is explicitly subject to review:

> **LEGAL_REVIEW_REQUIRED:** The Business Source License 1.1 (BSL 1.1) was
> evaluated as a starting point (see `LICENSING.md`). BSL 1.1 requires a
> Change License that is a "Later Applicable License" or a generally
> recognized open-source license and prohibits the Licensor from
> exercising any rights to the Licensed Work under non-open terms during
> the Change License window. If BSL 1.1 is adopted, its official text must
> be used unchanged together with the Licensor, Licensed Work, Change
> License and Change Date specifications. Until the legal review is
> complete, this section is a statement of intent only.

## 7. Third-Party Components

The software depends on third-party components with their own licenses
(notably Symfony components under the MIT license, Bootstrap under the MIT
license, Font Awesome, Laminas Mail, Z-Push and others). The respective
license and copyright notices of these components remain valid and are
documented in `NOTICE.md`. This license does not apply to third-party
components.

## 8. No Warranty and Limitation of Liability

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM,
DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR
OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE
OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.

> **LEGAL_REVIEW_REQUIRED:** Warranty and liability limitations must be
> aligned with mandatory law of the applicable jurisdiction (e.g. §§ 521 ff.,
> 536a BGB and the Product Liability Act for German law).

## 9. Governing Law

> **LEGAL_REVIEW_REQUIRED:** Choice of law and jurisdiction to be determined
> by legal counsel.

